    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nAll-New Audi A6 Allroad Estate Model Hits the Streets in this Region, and This Is How Much It Costs\n49 photos\nPhoto: Audi\nThe adventurer from the premium German brand from Ingolstadt, the Audi A6 Allroad, comes to the Land Down Under starting from AU$127,900, which is the equivalent of almost $90k at the current exchange rate.\nAudi in Australia has been pretty consistent with the novelties: in September they announced the refined Q6 e-tron and SQ6 e-tron models with better specifications and new pricing; in August they introduced to the range the all-electric Q4 e-tron models with improved technical specifications, and back in July they revealed the all-new Audi Q9 that is also coming to the Land Down Under .\nNow, in October, the fifth generation of the Audi A6 Allroad is coming to Australia with “a striking new wide-body design with the versatility, comfort, and capability synonymous with the Allroad nameplate.” For the local market, there will be two electrified powertrains, and it’s also the most “comprehensively equipped A6 Allroad to date, with standard adaptive air suspension, all-wheel steering, panoramic glass roof with switchable transparency, and next-generation digital technology.”\nAudi Australia has revealed the pricing and specification for the new iteration, which has been redesigned from the ground up alongside the regular A6 sedan and estate models, but comes as a more adventurous proposition with standard quattro all-wheel drive, adaptive air suspension, and all-wheel steering offered standard across the range.\nFor the Australian market, the family will have two siblings: A6 Allroad quattro e-hybrid, starting from AU$127,900, as well as the mild hybrid A6 Allroad TDI quattro , with pricing for the latter starting from AU$137,900, which is the equivalent of almost $97k at the current exchange rate.\nThe PHEV model combines the well-known 2.0-liter TFSI gasoline engine with an electric motor for a total combined output of 270 kW and 500 Nm. That’s 362 hp and 369 lb-ft of torque, by the way. There’s also a big 25.9 kWh battery pack, enabling an electric driving range of up to 87 km (54 miles), but it’s only combined with AC charging.\nThe e-hybrid is distinguished by the 21-inch Audi Sport alloy wheels and red brake calipers. The other option is the TDI quattro with a 3.0-liter turbo diesel and 220 kW plus 580 Nm (295 hp and 428 lb-ft) of torque, featuring Audi's latest mild hybrid plus technology.\nThe standard specification includes Matrix LED headlights and LED rear lights, while the optional Premium package adds digital Matrix LED headlights with micro-LED technology and digital OLED rear lights. Other perks include adaptive air suspension, all-wheel steering, the S Line interior, electrically adjustable front seats, a panoramic glass roof with switchable transparency, or the optional Customised contour seats package.\nThe technology package contains an 11.9-inch Audi virtual cockpit plus, a 14.5-inch OLED MMI touch display, as well as a standard 10.9-inch MMI front passenger display along with Audi connect plus, wireless Apple CarPlay and Android Auto, or a Bang & Olufsen 3D Premium Sound System, featuring 16 speakers, including a subwoofer, and a total output of 685 watts.\n\"The Audi A6 Allroad has always occupied a distinctive position in our portfolio, combining the practicality of an Avant with the confidence and capability of quattro all-wheel drive,\" said Peter Strudwicke, Audi Australia Product Manager for the A6 Allroad. \"This new generation takes that formula further, with a more striking, purposeful design, an exceptional level of standard equipment, and a sophisticated chassis that makes the A6 Allroad equally suited to everyday driving and longer journeys across Australia.\"\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2027 Audi A6 allroad Audi A6 Allroad Audi A6 allroad executive station wagon pricing Australia\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Chery Group International User Summit Features the World Premiere of the All-New Omoda X Adventurer",
